 "sports-field-turf": {
  "sections": [
   {
    "h2": "Published field projects give context, not a quote",
    "body": [
     "Aurora Public Schools' stadium field at Hinkley High School took 81,095 square feet of AstroTurf over a Brock Powerbase YSR shock pad with BrockFILL infill, completed in 2024. Riverside High School in Jacksonville, the first Duval County public school to get a synthetic playing surface, was reported at 91,000 square feet when it was unveiled on 18 October 2022. That is the working size of one high school field. These are outside projects, not Timeless installations or evidence of a price for your field.",
     "Nassau County publishes the contract value. On 27 February 2025 its school board approved a $1.7 million athletic facilities upgrade at West Nassau High School in Callahan, of which AstroTurf Corporation held the primary contract at $1,328,070. The scope was excavation of up to 7.5 inches of the existing surface, a drainage base, and turf with custom midfield logos and end-zone lettering under an eight-year manufacturer warranty."
    ],
    "sources": [
     {
      "label": "Brock USA project page — Aurora Public Schools Stadium, Hinkley High School",
      "cite": "81,095 sq ft artificial turf installation completed 2024 at APS Stadium, Hinkley High School, Aurora CO; AstroTurf surface with BrockFILL infill over a Brock Powerbase YSR shock pad; builder Rocky Mountain Turf Solutions, designer Design Concepts.",
      "url": "https://www.brockusa.com/projects/aurora-public-schools-hinkley-high-school-aurora-public-schools-stadium/",
      "checked": "2026-09-08"
     },
     {
      "label": "Duval County Public Schools — Riverside High School turf field",
      "cite": "Riverside High School was the first Duval County public school to receive an AstroTurf playing surface, unveiled 18 October 2022; reported as a 91,000-square-foot turf field.",
      "url": "https://www.duvalschools.org/article/2731211",
      "checked": "2026-09-08"
     },
     {
      "label": "Nassau County Record — Warrior Field renovation, West Nassau High School",
      "cite": "Nassau County School Board approved a $1.7 million athletic facilities upgrade at West Nassau High School (Callahan) on 27 February 2025; AstroTurf Corporation of Dalton, Georgia held the primary contract at $1,328,070; scope included excavation of up to 7.5 inches of field surface, installation of a drainage base, and new turf with custom midfield logos and end-zone lettering under an eight-year manufacturer warranty; ribbon cutting 5 September 2025.",
      "url": "https://www.nassaucountyrecord.com/local-newsletter/warrior-field-renovation-underway-west-nassau-high-school",
