    "h2": "Infill and workmanship are where these jobs separate",
    "body": [
     "Florida settled the infill question by rule. On a Florida single-family lot of one acre or less, Rule 62-308.100, F.A.C., effective 19 May 2026, limits infill to clean silica sand, rock, shell or other natural material, allows coated silica sand where the coating is non-toxic, and allows rubber or other synthetic infill only within the footprint of playground equipment. Commercial, multifamily, park and athletic-field work sits outside the rule.",
     "A Sports Health laboratory study found the time to 50 percent loss of MRSA viability ran 2 hours on EPDM rubber, 12 on crumb rubber, 13 on TPE and 27 hours on sand. On heat, a systematic review in the International Journal of Biometeorology reports Petrass and colleagues measuring SBR crumb rubber at 53.5 degrees Celsius against TPE at 45.6. A sand and organic infill plot in the same review measured 48.1 — a separate plot, not a head-to-head against those two.",
